WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.065 --> 00:00:12.625
So before you fix anything,

2
00:00:13.005 --> 00:00:14.265
find out what’s

3
00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:15.605
actually broken.

4
00:00:30.265 --> 00:00:31.985
Take KL Roasting Co.

5
00:00:32.345 --> 00:00:33.305
Great beans,

6
00:00:33.945 --> 00:00:34.665
flat sales.

7
00:00:35.265 --> 00:00:36.365
Last month’s promo worked

8
00:00:36.405 --> 00:00:37.225
for a week,

9
00:00:37.265 --> 00:00:38.265
then sales dropped

10
00:00:38.305 --> 00:00:39.185
right back.

11
00:00:39.465 --> 00:00:40.285
Now they want to cut

12
00:00:40.325 --> 00:00:41.425
the price for good.

13
00:00:41.845 --> 00:00:42.265
Don’t.

14
00:00:42.305 --> 00:00:42.945
Not yet.

15
00:00:43.221 --> 00:00:43.661
It starts

16
00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:45.281
with the BI Triangle.

17
00:00:58.628 --> 00:00:59.428
Here’s the thing.

18
00:00:59.688 --> 00:01:00.408
People don’t pay

19
00:01:00.448 --> 00:01:01.568
for what you are.

20
00:01:01.808 --> 00:01:02.968
They pay for what they think

21
00:01:03.008 --> 00:01:04.168
you are.

22
00:01:04.408 --> 00:01:05.208
Great beans,

23
00:01:05.528 --> 00:01:06.348
wrong outfit.

24
00:01:06.708 --> 00:01:08.508
But is it only the outfit?

25
00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:10.350
So we check everything.

26
00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.710
Each one scored out

27
00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:25.703
of ten.

28
00:01:25.797 --> 00:01:26.917
Most of it’s fine.

29
00:01:27.277 --> 00:01:28.437
Three score low.

30
00:01:28.877 --> 00:01:30.457
Now, the price theory.

31
00:01:31.217 --> 00:01:32.057
Rivals charge more,

32
00:01:32.097 --> 00:01:32.957
and still

33
00:01:32.997 --> 00:01:34.177
sell more.

34
00:01:34.217 --> 00:01:34.997
And the promo?

35
00:01:43.337 --> 00:01:44.917
The lowest is competition.

36
00:01:45.414 --> 00:01:46.594
The competition audit

37
00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:47.314
lines up

38
00:01:47.354 --> 00:01:48.534
every rival.

39
00:01:59.394 --> 00:02:00.614
We read the reviews.

40
00:02:01.174 --> 00:02:02.854
One word keeps coming back:

41
00:02:03.094 --> 00:02:03.754
stale.

42
00:02:04.274 --> 00:02:05.234
Now look at the shelf.

43
00:02:09.891 --> 00:02:11.331
When everyone says premium,

44
00:02:11.571 --> 00:02:12.811
nobody hears it.

45
00:02:12.851 --> 00:02:13.371
More ads

46
00:02:13.411 --> 00:02:15.091
would just shout it louder.

47
00:02:19.911 --> 00:02:21.051
Nobody owns it.

48
00:02:21.291 --> 00:02:22.431
And buyers are already

49
00:02:22.471 --> 00:02:23.971
asking for it.

50
00:02:24.011 --> 00:02:25.231
That’s the way in.

51
00:02:25.654 --> 00:02:26.734
And it gets worse.

52
00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:28.554
Even the name sounds

53
00:02:28.594 --> 00:02:29.854
like everyone else.

54
00:02:36.994 --> 00:02:37.834
Most names pass,

55
00:02:37.874 --> 00:02:39.334
and you keep yours.

56
00:02:39.754 --> 00:02:40.634
KL Roasting Co

57
00:02:40.674 --> 00:02:41.754
passes one.

58
00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:43.014
So this one’s

59
00:02:43.054 --> 00:02:43.994
a rename.

60
00:02:44.481 --> 00:02:45.921
First the rules,

61
00:02:46.301 --> 00:02:47.261
agreed before anyone

62
00:02:47.301 --> 00:02:48.641
has a favourite.

63
00:02:48.681 --> 00:02:50.141
Then a hundred new names

64
00:02:50.181 --> 00:02:51.481
take the same test.

65
00:02:51.841 --> 00:02:53.621
Half fail the first question.

66
00:02:54.001 --> 00:02:55.261
A first trade mark check

67
00:02:55.301 --> 00:02:56.361
cuts more.

68
00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:57.501
Four survive.

69
00:02:58.029 --> 00:02:59.689
Don’t pick a name off a list.

70
00:03:00.009 --> 00:03:00.869
Put it on a bag,

71
00:03:00.909 --> 00:03:02.069
on the shelf.

72
00:03:02.389 --> 00:03:03.669
That’s where you see it.

73
00:03:03.886 --> 00:03:04.996
The founders vote.

74
00:03:05.036 --> 00:03:06.266
Oriva wins,

75
00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:07.326
with the reasons

76
00:03:07.366 --> 00:03:08.366
on paper.

77
00:03:08.746 --> 00:03:10.546
Then the trade mark is filed.

78
00:03:11.406 --> 00:03:12.886
Registration takes about a year.

79
00:03:29.656 --> 00:03:30.316
And notice:

80
00:03:30.536 --> 00:03:32.236
nothing’s been designed yet.

81
00:03:32.436 --> 00:03:33.396
That’s the point.

82
00:03:33.816 --> 00:03:34.696
Now the money goes

83
00:03:34.736 --> 00:03:36.036
to the right fix.

84
00:03:36.722 --> 00:03:37.672
Oriva has a name,

85
00:03:37.712 --> 00:03:38.732
and a spot

86
00:03:38.772 --> 00:03:40.052
nobody owns.

87
00:03:40.092 --> 00:03:41.892
But what does it stand for?

88
00:03:42.212 --> 00:03:44.933
That’s Strategy.

